Rejected at STEP 0; no generator was built. The result is documented in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2605.29443/REJECTED.md).

- G and V are achievable by constructing and replaying legal move sequences.
- Track A fails: [Theorem 4.5](https://arxiv.org/html/2605.29443) proves move-calculus completeness, not hardness for generated random-walk endpoints.
- Track B fails: Proposition 4.4’s explicit CP certificate costs 20 moves mechanically and 20 moves via the compact route—there is no compression gap.
- Random-walk endpoints offer no paper-backed distributional hardness or shorter structural recovery method.

The rejection records the relevant theorems, both cost figures, easy regimes, and reconsideration criteria.
